A trap clears the mark another core's stop left but goes by its thread's state,
so a thread a call resumed between the stop and the trap runs on as the trap returns,
on registers a watcher may have written since, which under tracing the host cannot follow:
a traced core has its turn only for a thread the host follows, but while its trap is marked.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a traced core has its turn for a thread the host cannot follow
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-resume-before-trap

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -198,7 +198,6 @@ struct thread *core_trapped(void)
     /* A trap another core marked is not its thread's any more, whatever the thread is by then. */
     if (core->drop_trap) {
         core->drop_trap = false;
-        t = NULL;
     }
 #endif
     if (t != NULL && t->state == THREAD_READY) {
